# Witnesses for Higman--Sims Sylow double cosets

The 270 representatives are products of the existing stabilizer-chain words.
Counts on invariant sets of ordered pairs distinguish their double cosets.
Point colours bound the conjugate Sylow intersections, and generation words
exclude every representative outside the two local normalizers.

Source: ATLAS HSG1-p100B0 and Aschbacher--Smith A.3.12(18), pp.47--48.
The data are untrusted witnesses; descendant modules check every used identity.
